  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1159 AM CST SUN NOV 1 2026\n\nA bit of a dreary morning as we kick off November across Central\nAlabama. This morning has featured low level stratus and batches\nof light rain/drizzle at times. Over the last several hours, we\nhave seen the heaviest rainfall over North Alabama, where we have\nseen nearly 6\" of rain. Latest hi-res guidance suggests this\nactivity will fill in a bit more through the day as we reach peak\nheating. However, the bulk of today's action will stay north of\nus, closer to the passing upper level shortwave. This activity\nwill wane this evening as the shortwave lifts northeast as upper\nlevel ridging briefly nudges into the region.\n\nChances for showers and storms will return to the forecast\nTuesday evening as moisture pools ahead of our next system. A\nstout upper level trough will lift across the Plains towards the\nGreat Lakes region. Meanwhile, an associated surface low will\nkick a cold front our way by mid week. Look for breezy conditions\nahead of this front with gusts from 20-30 MPH likely. A line of\nshowers and storms ahead of this front will head our way Tuesday\nevening. Latest guidance suggests this activity will be losing\nsteam by the time it arrives across Central Alabama. While\ninstability will be limited, roughly 30 knots of shear would\nsupport a couple of isolated thunderstorms overnight Tuesday into\nWednesday morning. There is potential for this system to turn\ninto a flooding event for northwest portions of Central Alabama.\nAs the line of showers and storms pulls away from its support, it\nwill slow down as it moves across the Southeast. A healthy plume\nof PWATs and a developing ~40 knot H85 LLJ will help support\nperiods of heavy rainfall. Latest probabilities suggest a 50-60%\nchance of seeing at least 2\" of rain across our northwestern\ncounties overnight Tuesday through Wednesday. Activity will\ngradually come to an end Wednesday evening with some wrap around\nshowers possible on Thursday.\n\nAnother cold front pushes through the region on Friday. We aren't\nexpecting much in the way of precip with this one as our moisture\nwill be limited. A nice shot of cooler air will accompany this\nboundary with lows dropping back into the low to mid 40s next\nweekend.\n\n95/Castillo",
